# Machine-local settings for the dev scripts in this folder.
#
#   cp .env.local.example .env.local     (.env.local is gitignored)
#
# Every key is OPTIONAL. The scripts auto-detect devices and the LAN IP, and the
# repo root is derived from the script location, so a fresh clone needs none of
# this. Set a key only when you want to pin something.

# Where logcat / xptrace captures are written.
# Default: %LOCALAPPDATA%\quorum-mobile\captures
# Keep this OUTSIDE the repo. Captures can contain real key material, so a path
# inside a working tree risks it reaching a branch or a backup.
#QM_CAPTURE_DIR=D:\my-captures

# Checkout of the Quilibrium JS SDK, used by the dr-* protocol harnesses.
# Default: a sibling of this repo (../quilibrium-js-sdk-channels)
#SDK_DIR=D:\code\quilibrium-js-sdk-channels

# Pin adb device serials for the two-device scripts instead of auto-detecting.
# Find them with `adb devices`. Wi-Fi serials look like 192.168.x.x:5555
#QM_DEVICE_1=XXXXXXXXXXX
#QM_DEVICE_2=192.168.x.x:5555

# Pin the PC's LAN IP that Metro binds to, instead of auto-detecting it.
# Only needed if auto-detection picks the wrong adapter (VPN, multiple NICs).
#QM_HOST_IP=192.168.x.x

# ffmpeg binary, used by gen-launcher-webp.js to encode the launcher bitmaps.
# Default: C:\Program Files\ffmpeg\bin\ffmpeg.exe
# Set to just "ffmpeg" if it is on your PATH.
#QM_FFMPEG=ffmpeg

# ASCII-only temp dir for the native build scripts. AGP's C++/prefab staging
# runs under java.io.tmpdir; if your Windows profile name has a non-ASCII
# character it mangles and the NitroModules C++ build dies. Only change this if
# C:\Temp is unsuitable on your machine.
#QM_ASCII_TEMP=C:\Temp\
